PS5 HFR1 / CS2 Nuke / Expanded L3 CAT A/B/A
2026-11-07. Original CS2 -insecure, local Nuke 1x, first-person, seek 10048
(~02:38), server resume tick 12177 in every phase, 10-second warm-up,
reseek and 15-second measurement. System RADV 26.0.8, MP1 off, 1080p240 X11.
All scored notifications are Flip. FPS/tail metrics are displayed cadence.

A1/A2 used full ffff L3 masks, B 000f per domain for the same controlled class,
jointly allocating in 4 of 16 ways (1 MiB per domain). The group contained
154 Steam WebHelper threads and 78 Chromium renderer threads. Chromium GPU,
browser, zygote, audio/network utility processes, Codex and KDE session tasks,
CS2 and unrelated tasks stayed outside the group. Discord was absent from
the test. No CPU affinity or MB allocation changes. Root L3 stayed full.

B averaged about 0.92 displayed FPS more than the controls. Its 1% low and
P99 essentially matched A2. Chromium renderers registered no CPU ticks,
so this does not characterize an active Chromium workload or isolate a
Chromium-specific effect compared with the previous Steam-only experiment.
Counter snapshots are provided for context only.

Cleanup verified. CS2 closed and configs byte-identical. Test group removed,
resctrl unmounted, restore timer stopped. No new matching MCE/MSR/GPU/OOM
kernel events during the sequence.
Linux resctrl documentation: https://docs.kernel.org/filesystems/resctrl.html

